    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Oscillator strength measures the transition dipole moment $\\boldsymbol\\mu_{0n}$ between the ground state and state $n$, the matrix element of the dipole operator $\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\mu}=-\\sum_i\\hat{\\mathbf r}_i$ (atomic units):\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "f_n=\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\Delta E_n\\,\\lvert\\boldsymbol\\mu_{0n}\\rvert^2,\\qquad\n",
        "\\boldsymbol\\mu_{0n}=\\langle\\Psi_0|\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\mu}|\\Psi_n\\rangle=-\\int\\mathbf r\\,\\rho_{0n}(\\mathbf r)\\,\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf r\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "In $C_{1}$ every orbital is $a$ and every state $A$, so symmetry forbids no transition; only $f_n$ tells bright states from dark ones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Each bar stacks the weights of one state's transitions between orbital sets:\n",
        "\n",
        "- A transition's weight sums over its printed configurations; an unrestricted job counts $c_{ia}^2$ per spin instead of $2c_{ia}^2$:\n",
        "  $$\n",
        "  w=\\sum 2c_{ia}^2\n",
        "  $$\n",
        "- Configurations with $\\lvert c_{ia}\\rvert<0.1$ are not printed, so $\\sum w\\le 100\\,\\%$.\n",
